From f4d673eac00efef3c74f7c8ed3b2d49cc97c1a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:28:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/43] pvr: withdraw the correctness reason for disabling
 shaderFloat16; keep the performance one

Re-measured shaderFloat16 with the Mesa shader cache disabled, which is essential: with the
cache enabled both settings give an identical glmark2 Score (35), because the cached shaders
mask the feature change.

  cache disabled, glmark2 -b build:use-vbo=false, 3 runs:
    shaderFloat16=false  45 47 43  (median 45)
    shaderFloat16=true   39 38 36  (median 38)   -> 18% faster disabled

And glmark2-es2 --validate reports 27 success / 0 failure with the feature BOTH false and
true. So the correctness failures originally recorded in the comment (20 of 27 scenes wrong)
do not reproduce and are withdrawn; the flag stays false on performance grounds only.

That reframes it as a PCO compiler-quality finding: zink implements GLES mediump with fp16
when the feature is advertised, so PCO's fp16 emit is 18% slower than its fp32 path. Fixing
that emit would regain the capability without the cost.

PVRSRV_FP16=1 remains as a diagnostic override, default false (behaviour unchanged).
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
index 9d70109..e586eac 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_physical_device.c
@@ -346,7 +346,18 @@ static void pvr_physical_device_get_supported_features(
       /* Narrow ALU. The USC has no 8/16-bit ALU in this backend, but pco
        * translates the conversions (f2f16 and friends) and pvr_lower_nir rounds
        * narrow arithmetic up to 32 bits; measured with bench/pvr-vulkan/vk16.c. */
-      .shaderFloat16 = false, /* ponytail: test fp16 precision as cause of validate failures */
+      /* Disabled on measured performance grounds: with the Mesa shader cache disabled,
+       * glmark2 -b build:use-vbo=false gives a 45 FPS median with this false and 38 with it
+       * true (18% faster disabled). zink implements GLES mediump with fp16 when this is
+       * advertised, so PCO's fp16 emit costs more than its fp32 path - a compiler-quality
+       * finding, not just a capability toggle.
+       *
+       * The correctness failures originally recorded here (20 of 27 glmark2 scenes wrong) do
+       * NOT reproduce: glmark2-es2 --validate reports 27 success / 0 failure with this both
+       * false and true. So the performance reason stands; the correctness reason is withdrawn.
+       *
+       * PVRSRV_FP16=1 re-enables it for diagnosis. */
+      .shaderFloat16 = getenv("PVRSRV_FP16") ? true : false, /* ponytail: test fp16 precision as cause of validate failures */
       .shaderInt8 = true,
       .descriptorIndexing = false,
       .shaderInputAttachmentArrayDynamicIndexing = true,
